1. Aim
To perform active reconnaissance using the Recon-ng reconnaissance tool and gather information about a target domain.

2. Theory
Recon-ng is a free and open-source web reconnaissance framework written in Python. It is used for Open-Source Intelligence (OSINT) and information gathering during the initial phase of penetration testing.

Recon-ng provides an interactive command-line interface similar to Metasploit. It contains several modules that help security professionals collect information about a target domain, such as domain names, subdomains, IP addresses, DNS records, host information and other publicly available information.

Recon-ng provides a modular environment in which different modules can be installed and executed according to the requirements of the reconnaissance process.

It also provides features such as workspace management, module searching, module installation, database interaction, command completion and contextual help.

The workspace feature allows users to maintain separate environments for different targets. This helps organize the information collected during reconnaissance.

Recon-ng is mainly used during the information-gathering phase of ethical hacking and penetration testing.
Features of Recon-ng
1. Free and Open Source: Recon-ng is freely available and its source code can be accessed through GitHub.
2. Modular Framework: It provides different modules for performing various information-gathering activities.
3. Command-Line Interface: It provides an interactive command-line interface for executing reconnaissance commands.
4. Workspace Management: It allows users to create separate workspaces for different targets.
5. Subdomain Enumeration: It helps identify subdomains associated with a target domain.
6. DNS Information Gathering: It provides modules for collecting DNS-related information.
7. IP Address Discovery: It helps identify IP addresses associated with a target domain.
8. Database Interaction: It stores the collected reconnaissance information in an internal database.
9. Module Installation: Users can search, install and execute modules according to their requirements.
10. Information Gathering: It helps collect publicly available information about websites and organizations.
Uses of Recon-ng
1. To perform reconnaissance on a target domain.
2. To identify IP addresses associated with a domain.
3. To discover subdomains of a target website.
4. To collect DNS-related information.
5. To perform WHOIS information gathering.
6. To identify publicly available host information.
7. To collect information about web technologies.
8. To support vulnerability assessment and penetration testing.
9. To organize reconnaissance information using workspaces.
10. To identify potential attack surfaces during security assessments.




3. Procedure
Step 1: Open Kali Linux Terminal

Start Kali Linux and open the terminal.

Step 2: Download Recon-ng

Enter the following command to clone the Recon-ng repository from GitHub.
git clone https://github.com/lanmaster53/recon-ng.git


This command downloads the Recon-ng source code from GitHub into the local system.

Step 3: Launch Recon-ng

Enter the following command:
recon-ng


This launches the Recon-ng interactive console.

After successful execution, the Recon-ng prompt will appear.

Step 4: Create a Workspace

A workspace is a separate environment used to organize reconnaissance activities for a particular target.

First, view the available workspace commands:
workspaces


Create a new workspace:
workspaces create GeeksForGeeks


Here, GeeksForGeeks is the name of the workspace.

Step 5: Search for Available Modules

Enter the following command:
marketplace search


This command displays the available modules in the Recon-ng marketplace along with their installation status.

Step 6: Install Modules

To install a particular module, use:
marketplace install <module_name>


To install all available modules, use:
marketplace install all


This command installs the modules required for reconnaissance.

Step 7: Search for a Specific Module

Enter the following command:
modules search hack


This searches for installed modules containing the keyword hack.

In this experiment, the module used is:
recon/domains-hosts/hackertarget


Step 8: Load the Module

Enter the following command:
modules load recon/domains-hosts/hackertarget


This loads the Hackertarget module into the current workspace.

After loading the module, the command prompt changes to indicate that the selected module is active.

Step 9: Set the Target Domain

Before executing the module, specify the target domain.

Enter:
options set SOURCE google.com


Here:
- options set is used to configure module options.
- SOURCE specifies the target domain.
- google.com is the target domain used in the PDF.
Use only an authorized target or a domain permitted for testing.

Step 10: Execute the Module

Enter the following command:
run


This executes the loaded Hackertarget module against the specified domain.

The module collects available host and domain information and displays the results in the terminal.

The output may contain information such as:
- Hostname
- IP address
- Country
- Domain information
- Other discovered host details











Description

Recon-ng is a free and open-source reconnaissance tool written in Python. It is available on GitHub and can be used in Kali Linux through a command-line interface. Recon-ng is based on Open-Source Intelligence (OSINT) and is used to gather information about a target domain from publicly available sources. Its interface is similar to Metasploit, making it convenient for security professionals and penetration testers to perform reconnaissance.
Recon-ng provides a powerful environment for web-based information gathering. It contains various modules that help collect information about domains, hostnames, subdomains, IP addresses, and other publicly available details. These modules allow users to perform different reconnaissance tasks according to their requirements. The tool also provides interactive help, command completion, database interaction, and built-in functions that make information gathering easier.
One of the important features of Recon-ng is its workspace facility. A workspace provides a separate environment for conducting reconnaissance on different targets. It helps organize the information collected during an investigation and keeps the activities for different targets separate.
Recon-ng also provides a marketplace where users can search for and install modules. Each module performs a specific information-gathering task. After installing a suitable module, the user can load it, configure the required options, specify the target domain, and execute the module using the run command. The collected information can then be examined and documented.
Recon-ng can be used to gather domain-related information, discover subdomains, identify hostnames, perform DNS-related information gathering, and collect other details depending on the modules installed and the data sources available. It helps security professionals understand the publicly exposed information associated with a domain before conducting further security assessments.
The main advantage of Recon-ng is that it combines multiple reconnaissance functions in a single framework. Its modular structure allows users to select suitable modules for different tasks. It is useful for ethical hackers, penetration testers, and cybersecurity professionals during the information-gathering phase of security testing.
Thus, Recon-ng is an effective reconnaissance tool for gathering and organizing information about authorized target domains.


